    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>log</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></msub><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8226;</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;&nbsp; Column 1 contains information about zeros of <math> <mrow> <mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mi>x</mi> <mo>)</mo></mrow> </mrow> </math> , <math> <mrow> <mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mi>x</mi> <mo>)</mo></mrow> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>&#39;</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mi>x</mi> <mo>)</mo></mrow> </mrow> </math><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8226;</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;&nbsp; Column 2 contains information about the limiting behaviour of <math> <mrow> <mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mi>x</mi> <mo>)</mo></mrow> </mrow> </math> , <math> <mrow> <mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mi>x</mi> <mo>)</mo></mrow> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>&#39;</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mi>x</mi> <mo>)</mo></mrow> </mrow> </math> at infinity.<br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8226;</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;&nbsp; Column 3 contains information about increasing-decreasing nature of <math> <mrow> <mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mi>x</mi> <mo>)</mo></mrow> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo> <mi>x</mi> <mo>)</mo></mrow> </mrow> </math><table border=\"1\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Column 1</td>\t\t\t<td>Column 2</td>\t\t\t<td>Column 3</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(I) <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> for some <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(i) <math><mrow><mrow><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(P) <math><mi>f</mi></math> is increasing in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(II) <math><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#8242;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> for some <math><mi>x</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(ii) <math><mrow><mrow><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>&#8734;</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(Q) <math><mi>f</mi></math> is decreasing in <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(III) <math><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#8242;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> for some <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(iii) <math><mrow><mrow><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">lim</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>f</m